---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<Layout
  title="Probate & Estate Settlement"
  description="Probate and small estate affidavit document preparation in Grants Pass, Oregon — A1 Quality Paralegal."
>
  <section class="page-hero reveal">
    <div class="page-hero__inner">
      <h1>Settling an Estate Doesn't Have to Be Overwhelming.</h1>
      <p>Whether your situation calls for a simple affidavit or a full probate proceeding, we prepare the documents you need — clearly, accurately, and in person.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content reveal delay-1">
    <div class="content__inner">

      <h2>Understanding Your Options</h2>
      <p>When a loved one passes away, how their estate is handled depends on what documents they had in place and the value of what they left behind. Oregon law provides two main paths for estates without a trust:</p>

      <div class="packages__probate-callout">
        <strong>Oregon estate thresholds:</strong> Real property valued over $200,000 or cash assets over $75,000 typically require full probate. Estates below these thresholds may qualify for the simplified affidavit process. A properly established trust may help families avoid both.
      </div>

      <h2>Small Estate Affidavit</h2>
      <p>For qualifying smaller estates, Oregon law allows assets to transfer through a sworn affidavit rather than a full court probate proceeding. This is significantly faster and less costly than probate when the estate qualifies.</p>
      <p>A small estate affidavit — sometimes called a successor's affidavit — allows an heir to collect or transfer assets such as bank accounts, vehicles, or personal property by presenting the document directly to the institution holding the asset.</p>
      <p><strong>This may apply when:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Real property is valued under $200,000</li>
        <li>Cash and personal assets are under $75,000</li>
        <li>There is no trust in place</li>
        <li>You need to collect a specific asset on behalf of the estate</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Full Probate Document Preparation</h2>
      <p>When an estate exceeds the affidavit thresholds, Oregon law requires it to go through the formal probate process. This involves filing documents with the court, notifying creditors, and formally distributing assets according to the will or Oregon law.</p>
      <p>We prepare the documents needed at each stage, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Petition for appointment of personal representative</li>
        <li>Notice to interested parties</li>
        <li>Inventory and appraisement documents</li>
        <li>Final accounting and distribution documents</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>We Handle the Filing</h2>
      <p>We don't just prepare your probate documents — we handle all court filing on your behalf. You don't need to figure out which forms go where or navigate the county courthouse on your own. We take care of it from preparation through submission.</p>

      <div class="packages__probate-callout">
        <strong>Please note:</strong> Court filing fees are required by the court and are not included in our document preparation fee. We will let you know the applicable fees for your county at the time of your appointment.
      </div>

      <h2>Not Sure Which Applies?</h2>
      <p>Come sit down with us. We'll look at the situation together and help you understand which path makes sense — no guesswork, no legal jargon.</p>

      <h2>Planning Ahead</h2>
      <p>If you are handling a loved one's estate now, we can help. If you want to protect your own family from this process in the future, a properly established trust may be worth exploring. See our <a href={`${base}estate-planning/`}>Estate Planning packages</a>.</p>

      <div class="packages__cta" style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={`${base}contact-us/`}>Book an Appointment</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={`${base}contact-us/`} style="margin-left: 12px;">Ask a Question</a>
        <p class="packages__guarantee">If there is ever an error in your documents due to our preparation, we will correct it at no charge.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="assurance reveal delay-2">
    <div class="assurance__inner">
      <h2>We've Helped Grants Pass Families Since 1995.</h2>
      <p>Family owned and operated. We bring 30 years of experience, plain language, and personal attention to every case — especially the hard ones.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
